{"verdict": "accept", "reasons": ["No instance leakage: there are no hard-coded truth tables, instance ids, or lookups tied to one inventory. Everything is computed from view.H, view.alive, view.history, view.c, view.k and harness_lib.determined.", "No truth or IO access: the only import is harness_lib.determined, and the file reads no files, uses no network and runs no code outside the harness functions.", "Not degenerate: the claimed mechanism is actually implemented. build_feedback returns an empty string, filter_action vetoes repeated, determined or unparsable queries, compose_messages removes settled rejections, and final_hint lists the remaining configurations. This is a real change from bare, not just new constants or wording.", "Fits state_only: the veto covers only repeated or determined entries, which the regime allows. The list of undetermined outputs is the plain complement of the determined set in canonical order, with no ranking, split counts, information gain or recommended query. The final hint lists the remaining configurations, which is presenting state, not choosing a query.", "Bounded: filter_action returns None (accepts the reply) once one configuration remains or the query is informative. Rejected exchanges are removed from the context, so it stays about as short as bare's. The final list is capped at 15 configurations."], "risk_notes": ["The docstring says there are at most two re-asks per turn, but filter_action has no per-turn counter. That limit must come from the runner. If the runner has no cap, a model that keeps asking determined outputs would be re-asked without end.", "compose_messages matches vetoes by exact content and drops the assistant message just before each one. If an identical veto string appears again in a later turn, every earlier copy is also dropped (the intended behavior). The current exchange survives only because the range stops before the last message, so check that the runner always appends the veto as the last message before calling compose.", "When one configuration remains, final_hint gives the exact <guess> string. This is allowed under state_only as presenting the remaining configurations (alive), but most of the uniq@end/exact gain may come from this hint rather than from the veto. Compare it against a veto-only ablation without the hint, or against a parent that has the same final hint, before crediting the veto.", "The undetermined-output list can be long (c<<k entries, for example 24), and it appears only in veto messages that are later removed, so token cost is small. The tokens-per-episode claim depends on how the runner counts input tokens for re-asks."]}
```

